{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And his sons carried him.</b> Rashi explained: and not his grandsons, because they are from Canaanite women. But we say in Pesaḥim: what is 'the daughter of a Canaanite man' in the case of Judah? If you say an actual Canaanite — is it possible that Abraham came and warned Eliezer 'you shall not take a wife for my son from the daughters of the Canaanite,' and Isaac came and warned Jacob, and then Judah came and married one? Rather, what is 'Canaanite'? A merchant. And if you ask: according to the one who says regarding 'all his sons and all his daughters arose to comfort him' — twin sisters were born with each and every tribe, and they married them — why did his grandsons not carry him? One may answer: the twins died without children, and the tribes married Canaanite women and had children by them. And if you ask: why did the sons of Shimon not carry him, seeing that he came from that region, as it is written 'Yakhin and Tzoḥar and Sha'ul the son of the Canaanitess,' and we say: this is Dinah, who was violated by a Canaanite? One may answer: he did not want to arouse jealousy among them, that the sons of Shimon would carry him and not the sons of the other tribes. But from Efrayim and Menasheh, who carried him, there is no jealousy, since they were a king's sons, and additionally because they were established as tribes. And Rashi further explained: Levi did not carry, etc. And one should not ask: how did Moses carry the ark of Yosef? For he carried himself, as it is written 'He who leads like a flock Yosef' — and not that Moses carried him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {0 "In the phrase חז״ק הא אמרינן, the letter ק in חז״ק is unusual; the standard abbreviation is חז״ל. Translated as 'But' on the assumption that ק abbreviates קאמר or similar, introducing the counterpoint."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:28.236516627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}